  "body": "Found by the second review of PR #2664 (comment 7001940070). The PR is merged (c49d36762).\n\nWhat happens:\n- The fit keeps an edge that stands up to two pass tolerances (2 x 0.005 = 0.01 mm) off the surface (`crates/app/src/geometry/import/step_fit.rs:55`, `:162`).\n- `crates/app/src/geometry/import/step.rs:399` reports 0.005 mm as the chord error.\n- The fit does not measure the inside of a facet. On a sphere the inside can stand about 4/3 of the edge height off the surface.\n- On a cone and on a torus the edge midpoint is not exactly the worst point.\n- The worst case is about 0.013 mm of real error against 0.005 mm reported.\n\nWhy P3: the reported value is wrong, but it is below the usual tolerance. Verify uses the reported value.\n\nDone means: the import reports the largest measured height of the kept edges, with a bound for the facet inside. A test pins the value for a cylinder, a cone, a sphere and a torus.\n",
